{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts","id":232204,"title":"Changeling: The Lost, Second Edition Previews Thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-17T19:30:36-07:00","id":232204,"title":"Changeling: The Lost, Second Edition Previews Thoughts","content":"Excuse a little bluntness here. But I'm experimenting with how I'm going to Open Develop Changeling 2.0. <br /> <br /> So, right now I'm knee deep in work. I'm working on Forsaken 2e, Mage 2e, Requiem: Secrets of the Covenants, Beast: The Primordial, Promethean 2e, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand 2.0, Dark Ages V20, Armory: Hurt Locker and a few other things. Essentially, I'm writing a fuckton of words right now. <br /> <br /> I'm also leading some preliminary discussions on Changeling 2.0 (formerly Too Solid Flesh: The Huntsmen Chronicle). We've come up with some ideas I think are really keen and spot-on. I want to talk to you all about the game. But I want to frame these discussions, and get some input. I don't have a ton of time to spare, so I can't point-for-point discuss, debate, and rebut everything. I can't hope to answer every question. I will read them, but I can't promise responses. We also don't have the openness of scheduling that some past projects like Blood &amp; Smoke had. <br /> <br /> 1) There are some solid choices we're not really interested in changing or debating at length. For example, we have a pretty big change to the basic design assumptions surrounding Kiths and Seemings. Those are foundational changes, so fussing with them at this point would return us to Square One, and I can't do that to my team. <br /> <br /> 2) I basically have two ways I can engage in these discussions. I can favor formal, well-structured blog posts, which won't come very frequently, or I can favor sort of brainspew, stream of consciousness notes which would be more frequent. The thing is, a blog post is a thousand words that I have to compile and write. That's a big chunk of my day's work. If I don't plan it, I can just spout off a few things at a time. They will look a lot further from their final iterations. <br /> <br /> 3) It saves everyone a lot of time if nitpicking stays to a minimum. Not just with typographical errors and stuff (there's very little that bugs me more than people cracking on typographical errors I might make in stuff I'm posting without being paid, and which isn't going through a professionally paid editor). But really, harping on anything for too long distracts from productive discussion. If I say Dogs of Monstropolous have 34 teeth, but a previous edition reference says they have 32 teeth, it's fair to mention it. But somewhere around the tenth post talking about how the designers are so stupid for not knowing that the past edition referenced them having 32 teeth, we're really only patting each other on the back and discouraging productive conversation. <br /> <br /> 4) Read generously. Understand that most of what you'll see here is truncated from LONG email discussions, and rarely final draft material. <br /> <br /> 5) Understand that requests to rewrite large swaths of text are highly unlikely to bear fruit. We already do a couple of draft passes, where the writers are asked to clean up, rephrase, emphasize, example, and otherwise rework thousands of words. Anything they rewrite from the ground up has to go through all that again, without additional pay. It'd take a lot to get me to ask that of them. <br /> <br /> Anyway, that said, which would you prefer? Brain spew, or less frequent, more formal and intentionally framed posting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:42:36-07:00","id":232270,"title":"","content":"I'd favor brainspew.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I think Dave Brookshaw has done a pretty good job in the time leading up to FWC's devblogs with his informal spoilers. While I can't read his mind or divine exactly how he did it, it seemed like people posted in threads asking questions and speculating, and whatever quick thing Dave was ready to discuss, he'd answer briefly with that in a thread.<br /> <br /> Doing that sort of loose Q&amp;A where the questions you're ready/interested in answering can be answered might be a more time effective way to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:46:21-07:00","id":232276,"title":"","content":"Brain spew, because I'm impatient and so I want more information faster with fewer gaps.<br /> <br /> And because I'm impatient so I want you working on that, frankly, insane amount of material you're working on. All of which I'm excited about. A lot.<br /> <br /> Also, because I feel like brainspew is better for development until the very end when its really just teasing stuff (like Mage is doing). If you want thoughts on something, you can just make a quick post about it instead of the big production a blog post would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:51:13-07:00","id":232282,"title":"","content":"I also vote brainspew!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:51:16-07:00","id":232283,"title":"","content":"I accept your terms! Erm, I mean... alright, I'll be good. Promise. Understanding and helpfulness dialed up all the way to maximum. Criticism dialed back and loaded up with constructive sugar. Yes.<br /> <br /> As to the question of quick blurbs/more formal posting... I see pro's and cons to both:<br /> <br /> Formal blogs: More structured, less chance of things being taken out of a larger context by people, etc...<br /> Stream-of-consciousness: Faster, less work, makes everyone feel a bit more involved... and it sounds like you want to do this option. I think that last bit is reason enough to do it.<br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of Fail Faster for creative work. The faster you share material, the rawer it is, the more useful feedback will generally be to you, and the less effort is 'wasted'. As you said, when things have been established and worked out you &quot;can't do that to your team&quot;, even if someone were to bring up something completely valid. That's understandable, and totally accepted. I vote for short blurbs because it sounds like it'll be less work for you, and at the same time more useful. (I know it's not a vote, don't mind the terminology <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Also, it'll stirr up the discussions and speculation on changeling 2.0 frequently, rather than let it stagnate for longer periods, which is healthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:59:36-07:00","id":232298,"title":"","content":"I'll go for Fail Faster too. Voting Brainspew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T20:02:32-07:00","id":232304,"title":"","content":"Given what you have to deal with, I'd say brain spew is the most practical. Take what time you can and just get it out in bits, manage the work in loads that make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T20:11:03-07:00","id":232312,"title":"","content":"Another Brainspew Vote for the pile, speaking from the position of having become intimately familiar with how much more difficult it is to deal with larger parceled infopackets compared to smaller ones in the last month or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T00:40:35-07:00","id":232563,"title":"","content":"If you're doing brainspew, I'd suggest linking to this thread on each one to reiterate points like no nitpicking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T00:43:23-07:00","id":232564,"title":"","content":"Brainspew, please. Especially with Moar Numbered Lists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:06:51-07:00","id":232580,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m assuming the brainspews won out. If not, I\u2019m voting for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T01:08:25-07:00","id":232585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=232563#post232563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're doing brainspew, I'd suggest linking to this thread on each one to reiterate points like no nitpicking.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Done and done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:08:36-07:00","id":233047,"title":"","content":"I throw mine in for brain spew. Are there any fundamental changes youre allowed to share already? Im eager to see some minor rebalancing (autumn court mantle, im lookin at you) and other streamlining of the game, cant wait to see what you guys have in store. The 2.0 team is brilliant, I love what theyre sharing so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:45:46-07:00","id":233200,"title":"","content":"This is either going to end very well or very, very poorly. If you're going this rout, then Brainspew is definitely the best option. I would make sure you have a mod or two moderating these threads so they stay on target and productive, while seperating yourself from being &quot;the bad guy&quot; when things go out of hand. Also please be clear on <i>exactly</i> what you want discussed. If you post a long five page essay on a big concept and then put a two line section on something only semi-related I promise you that forumites will ignore your 5 page essay for the two lines [/hyperbole].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:19:51-07:00","id":233380,"title":"","content":"Can I vote? If so, I vote for brainspew, too. It'll be more helpful to the whole team in the long run, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T00:14:04-07:00","id":242879,"title":"","content":"So, when do we get our second brainspew? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T03:12:11-07:00","id":242951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=242879#post242879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, when do we get our second brainspew? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ask, and if I was going to do it anyway, you shall receive! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts\"> Changeling 2.0 Brainspew 2: Contracts - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Right now, we're chattering over Contract structure. The way it looks, they're going to come in four flavors: Universal Contracts This is a Contract. It has a </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T01:02:01-07:00","id":244660,"title":"","content":"This is a response to something in the Contracts branspew thread that I thing fits better here. I feel like speculating on what Courts represent in Changeling 2.0<br /> <br /> <br /> My theory is that:<br /> <br /> Kith is what your Keeper did to you.<br /> Seeming is how you regained agency.<br /> Courts are what you use that agency for / where you go next.<br /> <br /> <br /> I say &quot;my theory&quot; but this is really me taking the obvious guess; as that's what Courts always were in Changeling 1.0. Even if it could have been explained a bit better. (E.G: Spring was building a new human life, Autumn was builidng a new faerie life)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T05:35:43-07:00","id":244753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=244660#post244660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a response to something in the Contracts branspew thread that I thing fits better here. I feel like speculating on what Courts represent in Changeling 2.0<br /> <br /> <br /> My theory is that:<br /> <br /> Kith is what your Keeper did to you.<br /> Seeming is how you regained agency.<br /> Courts are what you use that agency for / where you go next.<br /> <br /> <br /> I say &quot;my theory&quot; but this is really me taking the obvious guess; as that's what Courts always were in Changeling 1.0. Even if it could have been explained a bit better. (E.G: Spring was building a new human life, Autumn was builidng a new faerie life)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great guess, but totally not the case. <br /> <br /> I'll chatter on Courts soon. If you want to speculate a little more, think reclamation as aegis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T09:02:26-07:00","id":244832,"title":"","content":"I'd say 1.0 courts were more coping mechanisms and the stages of grief.<br /> <br /> Spring was Denial, pretending you're fine and partying away the pain.<br /> Summer was Anger, what it says on the tin.<br /> Fall was Bargaining, both in the literal sense (thats what contracts are) and in the sense that you're attempting to regain control of yourself, faeness included.<br /> Winter was Depression, again, what it says on the tin.<br /> Courtlessness is Acceptance, you finally move beyond the need for the established structures to help you manage yourself and stand on your own.<br /> <br /> As for 2.0?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=244753#post244753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to speculate a little more, think reclamation as aegis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea right now. Aegis makes me think they'll still be related to coping/defense mechanisms, but seeing as now there's going to be a much more focus on other Court systems, they probably won't be as limited as in 1.0. Color me interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T14:18:56-07:00","id":244991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=244753#post244753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll chatter on Courts soon. If you want to speculate a little more, think reclamation as aegis.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have to admit the focus on reclamation makes me a bit nervous - none of my charachters have tried to reclaim their old life (I play Autumn).<br /> <br /> I guess I'll find out either way soon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=244832#post244832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say 1.0 courts were more coping mechanisms and the stages of grief.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually that's just a coincidence - the authors have said they never intended that (but were happy when it turned out the Seaosnal Courts fit that well). I don't think that the Courts were ever given a core one sentence desciption of their intent, but I've found that &quot;where you go next&quot; works best.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-30-2014, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T16:12:41-07:00","id":245051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=244991#post244991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have to admit the focus on reclamation makes me a bit nervous - none of my charachters have tried to reclaim their old life (I play Autumn).<br /> <br /> I guess I'll find out either way soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can't say for sure if MachineIV meant this, but I don't think so much was meant reclaiming your OLD life, as just your life AT ALL. Like, getting home is half the battle, but now how do you fit in? How do you find your way in a world that never knew you were gone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T07:36:36-07:00","id":245326,"title":"","content":"Even by that definition I wonder how Summer and Winter will fit in. I always interpreted those two courts as being less about claiming/reclaiming a life and more about making sure you never go back to slavery.<br /> <br /> Winter by hideing, Summer by learning to fight back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T10:49:01-07:00","id":246235,"title":"","content":"Changelings are hunted creatures. Fairyland isn't the kind of place that just lets a person leave without consequences. Even if a changeling's Keeper and its loyalists aren't actively searching for them, there are other things in the Hedge that will try to exploit and subvert the agency of any Lost that they come across. It really is hard to get back to your &quot;real life&quot; on Earth when you are constantly looking over your shoulder, on the run and harried by the huntsman's horn and the howls of briarwolves. That is why you join a Court, because a Court and its freehold allows you the freedom to actually live your life on your own terms. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T12:01:27-07:00","id":246287,"title":"","content":"&quot;Reclamation as aegis&quot;... I keep thinking of someone attending weight watchers or AA meetings - like how you are living a new life, new rules, a new identity - when you join a court you are committing to a new way of living to protect yourself and reidentify yourself..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T23:21:40-07:00","id":472262,"title":"","content":"My group didn't see the courts as the stages of coping, but rather the common paths the abused take in life. Spring is turning to hedonism, Summer represents revenge fantasies and lashing out, Fall is perpetuating the cycle by replicating the abuse, and Winter is the denial of the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4149-xeros97","name":"Xeros97","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T16:41:22-07:00","id":473505,"title":"","content":"I vote for brainspew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:59:16-07:00","id":473621,"title":"","content":"I could definitely go for more brainspew or something, to be honest. It's been a long while since we've had an update and I've been thinking about Changeling a lot lately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:21:49-07:00","id":473656,"title":"","content":"Same. Lost 1.0 was lightning in a bottle so this update is the one I'm most nervous about by far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:23:30-07:00","id":473662,"title":"","content":"Are we seriously still voting for the thing Dave decided on ages ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:40:35-07:00","id":473680,"title":"","content":"Just the first person. I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:42:47-07:00","id":473791,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it looked like you and SoulGambit read it as less, &quot;I vote for the creation of brainspews,&quot; than, &quot;I vote for a new brainspew.&quot; Understandable, as the ones we got were a lot of fun. It feels like Dave's been too busy to share more details for a while, too.<br /> <br /> I saw from the Morning meeting updates that C:tL 2nd edition entered redlines a few weeks ago. I'm curious about how the first drafts went over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:12:32-07:00","id":474529,"title":"","content":"I knew what they meant. But rather than harp on the fact that the vote was done, I decided it was a decent place to nudge the sentiment forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:16:11-07:00","id":475166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=473791#post473791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it looked like you and SoulGambit read it as less, &quot;I vote for the creation of brainspews,&quot; than, &quot;I vote for a new brainspew.&quot; Understandable, as the ones we got were a lot of fun. It feels like Dave's been too busy to share more details for a while, too.<br /> <br /> I saw from the Morning meeting updates that C:tL 2nd edition entered redlines a few weeks ago. I'm curious about how the first drafts went over.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're going good. I've been a bit distant, because I've got some intense shit going on in my life right now. But, things are moving along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:53:50-07:00","id":475197,"title":"","content":"Oosh. I'm happy to hear development on the line is going well, but significantly less happy about whatever hand life's dealt you lately. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Here's hoping the storm clouds depart sooner than later, and please stay as distant as you find it helpful to manage things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:58:52-07:00","id":475206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=475166#post475166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're going good. I've been a bit distant, because I've got some intense shit going on in my life right now. But, things are moving along.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to hear that. Whatever it is I hope it passes soon!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T21:24:41-07:00","id":475351,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on Changeling 2e? As in how this should probably go? As someone who bought literally every CTL product up till this point...<br /> <br /> -Buff them mechanically - particularly, make Contracts more versatile in general - but not in comparison to the Gentry, who should be as terrifying as always. (Personally, I think a single Changeling should generally be more powerful than a single Vampire.)<br /> -Clarify Pledge rules, but ensure they remain exceedingly flexible.<br /> -Reversing Kiths and Seemings works because everyone used Dual Kith anyway - this alteration in and of itself is just swell, actually. The core ideas of what Seemings and Kiths represented, however, were perfectly sound and do not require any alteration. Mechanically speaking, however, some Kiths were obviously just better than their peers (lol Shadowsoul and Whisperwisp) and they should be better balanced against each other. Granted, this may not even be a problem within the new structure at all.<br /> -Have the corebook be more organized and written with the knowledge of the information introduced in Equinox Road, particularly with regards to the True Fae. This information does not need to be spelled out as explicitly as it was in Equinox Road, despite that book being spectacular, although it of course warrants exposition in a later book. There is just something of a disconnect between the True Fae as portrayed in Autumn Nightmares with their nature in Equinox Road, and the 1e corebook errs closer to Autumn Nightmares, likely due to them being earlier in the development cycle.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, there is no need to screw with anything else. No need to change their themes. No need to alter their themes even the slightest bit. No need to give the Lost more or less agency. No need to focus more or less on any of a Changeling's struggles - with the Gentry, with the Courts, or with themselves. No need whatsoever to spin CTL in a new fashion. It was right the first time.<br /> <br /> Of course, with those &quot;foundational changes&quot; of yours, it's difficult to know how much of this post will actually matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1857-nahash","user":"Nahash","date":". 04-10-2015, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1857-nahash","name":"Nahash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:18:24-07:00","id":476230,"title":"","content":"Dave,<br /> <br /> Glad the game is progressing well. Hope life starts turning your way. Will pray and send good wishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T17:40:05-07:00","id":476469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nahash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232204-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-previews-thoughts?p=475351#post475351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on Changeling 2e? As in how this should probably go? As someone who bought literally every CTL product up till this point...<br /> <br /> -Buff them mechanically - particularly, make Contracts more versatile in general - but not in comparison to the Gentry, who should be as terrifying as always. (Personally, I think a single Changeling should generally be more powerful than a single Vampire.)<br /> -Clarify Pledge rules, but ensure they remain exceedingly flexible.<br /> -Reversing Kiths and Seemings works because everyone used Dual Kith anyway - this alteration in and of itself is just swell, actually. The core ideas of what Seemings and Kiths represented, however, were perfectly sound and do not require any alteration. Mechanically speaking, however, some Kiths were obviously just better than their peers (lol Shadowsoul and Whisperwisp) and they should be better balanced against each other. Granted, this may not even be a problem within the new structure at all.<br /> -Have the corebook be more organized and written with the knowledge of the information introduced in Equinox Road, particularly with regards to the True Fae. This information does not need to be spelled out as explicitly as it was in Equinox Road, despite that book being spectacular, although it of course warrants exposition in a later book. There is just something of a disconnect between the True Fae as portrayed in Autumn Nightmares with their nature in Equinox Road, and the 1e corebook errs closer to Autumn Nightmares, likely due to them being earlier in the development cycle.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, there is no need to screw with anything else. No need to change their themes. No need to alter their themes even the slightest bit. No need to give the Lost more or less agency. No need to focus more or less on any of a Changeling's struggles - with the Gentry, with the Courts, or with themselves. No need whatsoever to spin CTL in a new fashion. It was right the first time.<br /> <br /> Of course, with those &quot;foundational changes&quot; of yours, it's difficult to know how much of this post will actually matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't far off. Although, we're treating Gentry more as plot devices than anything in 2e; they're not getting a ton of depth in the core. <br /> <br /> But we are mechanically and stylistically making it in line with Second Edition. That means more in some places, less in others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T07:14:46-07:00","id":476930,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts and questions:<br /> <br /> I'm a bit curious about the role Huntsmen play. What do they provide that a Loyalist or Gentry can't? I checked out the outline and am getting a bit of a &quot;relentless persuer&quot; vibe. Is that more or less their niche? If so, how does it differ from the way the Gentry filled that role in 1E?<br /> <br /> You mentioned that 2E is going to be shifting Changeling from an abuse metaphor to a survivor metaphor. One of the things (I feel) that made 1E work as well as it did was the strength of that metaphor and the impressive level of maturity it was handled with. How do you feel the transition has affected this? What doors does this transition open? What, if any, doors does it close?<br /> <br /> What's your favorite thing about The Huntsman Chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}